# SRG-APP-001035-AU-000430  -  CAT I
# The Central Log Server must be a version supported by the vendor.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-001035-AU-000430
group:           V-278989
severity:        high
cat:             CAT I
determination:   ORGANIZATIONAL
grade:           C
decidable:       manual
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-003376
control_rev5:    SA-22

contribution:    Splunk Enterprise makes its own installed release identifiable through the
                 product's own interfaces (the CLI version command and the server
                 information REST endpoint), so the application supplies the release and
                 build identifier an assessor compares against the vendor's published
                 support policy, but it exposes no setting that sets, constrains, or
                 attests the support status of that release.

external:        Software deployment that fixes the installed release: the container image
                 build or package installation pins the Splunk Enterprise release and
                 build, and rebuilding or reinstalling is the only action that changes
                 support status.
external:        Splunk Enterprise software maintenance and support entitlement held for
                 the installed release (vendor contract), which the application cannot
                 record or enforce.
external:        Organizational software lifecycle and patch management procedure
                 establishing the supported-release baseline and the trigger to upgrade
                 before vendor end of support.
external:        The vendor's published Splunk Enterprise support policy and end-of-support
                 dates for the installed release train, which the application does not
                 carry and cannot evaluate.

manual_reason:   Support status is a property of the installed release and of the
                 maintenance entitlement held for it, not of configuration. checks.tsv
                 assigns no conf, stanza, or key to this requirement, and an independent
                 sweep of all 67 Splunk 10.4.2 *.conf.spec files found no key that governs,
                 reports, or attests vendor support or release currency: the only
                 version-adjacent keys are web.conf.spec:192-196 (updateCheckerBaseURL, a
                 Splunk.com release-notification URL that may be set to 0),
                 app.conf.spec:116-119 (show_upgrade_notification, a per-app Splunk Web
                 notice, default false), and limits.conf.spec:3556-3559
                 (version_upgrade_max_start_retries and the sibling version_upgrade_* keys,
                 documented as internal KV Store migration and upgrade settings not to be
                 changed except on vendor instruction). A phrase sweep of the same
                 specification set for end-of-life, end-of-support, EOL, vendor support,
                 and supported release returns zero hits. Deciding this requirement
                 requires reading the installed package's release, which is not Splunk
                 configuration, so no condition in the criterion vocabulary can be written
                 over it.

citation:        Central Log Server SRG V3R5, SRG-APP-001035-AU-000430 (V-278989), severity
                 high, CCI-003376, SA-22 a: check text "Verify that the Central Log Server
                 is a version supported by the vendor"; fix text "Upgrade or install a
                 Central Log Server which is a version supported by the vendor." No product
                 STIG rule shares CCI-003376; the sunset Splunk Enterprise 8.x for Linux
                 STIG V2R3 states the same requirement under SPLK-CL-000510 (V-274465,
                 CCI-002605) with fix text "Upgrade to a version supported by the vendor.",
                 naming no configuration value. Specification basis for the absence of a
                 setting: web.conf.spec:192-196, app.conf.spec:116-119,
                 limits.conf.spec:3556-3559.
finding:         This determination is made from the perspective of the application layer
                 alone: Splunk Enterprise exposes no configuration setting that establishes
                 or attests vendor support for its own release, so the application's share
                 of this requirement is limited to reporting the installed release and
                 build, and a finding is sustained only where the release the instance
                 reports is at or past the vendor's published end of support, remedied by
                 installing a supported release through the deployment rather than by any
                 configuration change.
